From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kennytech73 <contact@bookworm-mon0.org>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 08:15:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/cix: dptx: audio: announce the real sampling frequency
 in the channel status

The DP controller takes the IEC 60958 channel status byte that carries
the sampling frequency and the clock accuracy
(TRILIN_DPTX_SEC0_CS_FREQ_CLOCK_ACCURACY) with the first transmitted bit
in bit 0. The DPTX_CS_SAMPLING_FREQ_* values are written in transmission
order, first bit on the left, so the byte reaches the sink bit-reversed:
a 48 kHz stream (0x40) is announced as 44.1 kHz, and only 44.1 kHz
(0x00) is announced correctly.

Displays ignore the channel status and play the stream anyway. HDMI
capture devices trust it: an Elgato 4K S behind the on-board DP to HDMI
converter (Parade PS186) passes the sound through to its HDMI output but
captures silence at 48 kHz, the default rate of PipeWire.

Reverse the bits of that byte before writing it. The word length /
original frequency byte (TRILIN_DPTX_SEC0_CS_LENGTH_ORIG_FREQ) is taken
as written by the controller and is left alone: reversing it too gives
a distorted capture at 44.1 kHz.

Tested on an Orange Pi 6 Plus with the Elgato 4K S as HDMI sink:
32 kHz (0x03), 44.1 kHz (0x00) and 48 kHz (0x02) are captured cleanly,
sound on the display unchanged. Higher rates follow the same rule but
are not tested (not accepted by this sink).

[added by BOOKWORM]
---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_dptx_audio.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_dptx_audio.c
index 0119509f017fd2e24a788e67c033d75f8d74bbaa..bcb1a0a5a1d889749e7101958d6c6e7798588fd1 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_dptx_audio.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_dptx_audio.c
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
 /* Copyright 2024 Cix Technology Group Co., Ltd. */
+#include <linux/bitrev.h>
 #include <linux/kernel.h>
 #include <linux/hdmi.h>
 #include <drm/drm_eld.h>
@@ -84,8 +85,16 @@ static void dptx_audio_setup(struct trilin_dp *dp, int source, int freq,
 
 	trilin_dp_write(dp, TRILIN_DPTX_SEC0_CS_LENGTH_ORIG_FREQ + offset,
 			cs_length_orig_freq);
+	/*
+	 * The controller takes this channel status byte (sampling frequency
+	 * and clock accuracy) with the first transmitted bit in bit 0, while
+	 * the DPTX_CS_SAMPLING_FREQ_* values are written in transmission
+	 * order. Written as is, 48 kHz (0x40) is announced as 44.1 kHz:
+	 * displays do not care, HDMI capture devices mute the stream.
+	 * The word length / original frequency byte above is taken as is.
+	 */
 	trilin_dp_write(dp, TRILIN_DPTX_SEC0_CS_FREQ_CLOCK_ACCURACY + offset,
-			cs_freq_clock_accuracy);
+			bitrev8(cs_freq_clock_accuracy));
 	/* copyright*/
 	trilin_dp_write(dp, TRILIN_DPTX_SEC0_CS_COPYRIGHT + offset,
 			DPTX_CS_COPYRIGHT);
